<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan sells 60,000/T July fuel oil at $100.50/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan sells 60,000/T July fuel oil at $100.50/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has sold by tender 60,000-tonnes of July 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil at about $100.50 per tonne on a free-on-board (fob) basis, a CPC official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The two 180-centistoke 30,000 tonne cargoes sold, are lifting in the first half of July from Kaohsiung, the official said.</p>
<p>The tender closed on June 10 and was valid for two days.</p>
<p>CPC sold three 30,000-tonne cargoes of 3.0-percent sulphur fuel oil in its previous tender for June lifting at around $100 per tonne, fob Kaohsiung.  </p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3571)</p>
</text>
